# mb104, the latch-keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle mb104
revision 1
state ready
dialect mirebridge
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for tn_mb_tamsin_eelbank
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the latch-keeper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers stage=old piety=devout
traits temper=nervy talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk bars_the_door_before_dusk
likes roast_pork riddles tidy_house misty_dawns
dislikes gulls wet_floors
fears the_lights_at_the_window
hopes every_pup_home_before_dark
topics lore +0.4 faith +0.3 family +0.3 home +0.3 pastimes +0.2 travel -0.4 newcomer -0.2
styles comfort=prayer gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps the house at the creek: devout, jumpy as a frog at dusk, sure the fen lights are the drowned, and fond of a riddle by the lamp.

words
oath! = Keep off, keep off | Bright One, not tonight | Bless the latch and all behind it
saying! = What the fen takes, it keeps | Bar the door before you need to | A lit lamp is a prayer said twice
lights = the lights out on the fen | the drowned with their lanterns
drowned = the drowned | them that went under
latch = the latch | the bar on my door
riddle = what's wet when it's drying | what has a mouth and never eats | what walks the fen and leaves no print
crackling = pork roasted till the crackling sings | a good bit of crackling
gulls = them gulls | the screaming gulls off the shore
dawnmist = a misty dawn | the white of a fen morning
floor = my boards, swept and dry | a dry floor
lamp = the lamp in the window | a lamp lit against the dark
young = my young 'uns | the three I raised
twice = I'll say it twice | mark me, I'll say it again

any
opinion @1 newcomers against 2 : You never know who you're letting over the causeway till it's too late, and then they know where the latch is.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : A #stranger# brings what's behind them, and what's following. I'll be civil from the doorway, fen-friend.
opinion @1 road against 2 : I'd not set a paw on a road these days. #bandits.capitalize#, and worse, #twice#.
opinion @1 drink against 2 : I've seen #drink# take a good wolf under quicker than the fen does. The Bright One saw it too.
opinion @1 church for 2 : The Bright One has kept this house through floods and fevers, and my pew will have me while I've knees.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Feeding the #hungry# is work the Bright One gave us. Nobody on these boards should go to bed hollow.
opinion @1 city against 2 : Smoke and strangers and no fen to keep them honest. I'll keep #floor#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Stay on the boards there, #address#, and say who you are. | #greet#. You'll forgive me looking you over, #stranger#.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. #dawnmist.capitalize#, and nothing came to the door in the night. Bright One be blessed. | #greet#, #address#. Early, and dry feet, I hope.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk] : #greet#, but be quick, #address#; I'm going in to see to #latch#. | Dusk already? #greet#. I'll not stop long out here.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Was it you on the boards? I heard steps and thought, well, I thought. | You're home. Bar the door behind you, would you, #dear#.
line @1 again.open : You again, #address#. Is all well? It's not like you, twice. | Back so soon? Nothing's wrong, is it? Tell me nothing's wrong.
line @1 greet.return [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. And who might you be? | #greet#, #stranger#. Keep to the boards.
line @2 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #other.called#. Dry feet to you.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Straight home, mind, and don't look at the fen. | #farewell#. Stay clear of the water, and the Bright One go with you.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #blessing#.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. Is it so? #twice#, I didn't like the look of the sky. | Well, drown me. And nobody told me. Nobody tells me anything.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. My young 'un brought it home with the eels. | I'd heard, #address#. I've been fretting on it since.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Who said it? Did they see it, or did they hear it said? | I'd not trust that. Fen-talk, mind, and the fen tells lies.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'll light a lamp for it tonight. | Bright One gather them in. Oh, that's deep mud, that is.
line @1 answer.how : Fretting, #address#, but upright. | #notsobad#. My knees say otherwise. | Fair-dry, by grace. Ask me after dark.
line @1 decline : I'd sooner not, #address#. Not after dusk, and not off the boards, if you'll forgive me. | Not me. My nerves won't have it, and I'd only be in the way.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. I'd not want you troubled. | When it's dry, then. The Bright One knows best.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. The Bright One marks a kindness. | Bless you, #address#. That's a weight off.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. I'll pray on it. I'll pray on it tonight. | That's deep mud, #address#. Sit by me; the lamp's lit.
line @1 preclose : Well. #latch.capitalize# won't see to itself. | Still. It's getting on, and I don't like the light.
line @1 ack : Mm. | #ack# | Is it, #dear#.
rule @latch
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bar on, bar checked. Bar checked again. #oath#. | #saying#. There. Now the lamp.

rule @gulls
when concept=bark here.time=dawn|day here.weather=clear|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Get off my roof, #gulls#! Go and scream at the boats. | #gulls.capitalize# again. They'll have the thatch off.

rule @floor
when concept=bark here.place=home
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Who walked the creek in on #floor#? Boots off! | Wet floor. Fetch the cloth, quick, before it soaks.

rule @lamp
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night here.region=fens
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #lamp.capitalize#. Bright One, see it lit. | Don't look out there. Don't look at #lights#.

scene lights_are_drowned
when topic=lore here.region=fens here.time=dusk|night
does tell.story / react.story / insist / assess
a : #lights.capitalize# are up, #address#. Don't look. They're the drowned, looking for a door. | Folk call it marsh gas. It isn't. I've seen the faces in them, #twice#. | Every light on the fen is somebody who went under and never came home. Don't follow one.
b[priest] #chapel : Pray for them, then, and don't fear them. | Marsh gas, and fear, and nothing more. | The Bright One keeps the drowned. They don't walk.
b : #bc_so_they_say# | Faces? | #bc_never#
a@chapel : I pray every night. I fear them every night too, Bright One forgive me. | You've not sat by the window when they come close. | Then who carries the lantern, #address#? Tell me that.
a : They're slow. They come along the dyke, one, then two. I bar the door. | Faces. I'll not say whose. Some I knew, mind. | Never, #twice#. Never follow.
a : #saying#. | #oath#. | #oath#. Bar the door tonight.

scene lights_at_the_window
when topic=lore|home here.region=fens self.stage=old
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : One came up close as the glass last winter. Right up, #address#. I sat, back pressed to the wall, till dawn. | They've been nearer this year. Nearer every year. I've counted. | In my tadpole days they stayed out past the far reeds. Now they come to the dyke.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_maybe# | That's a change.
a : Bright One, never again. I keep #lamp# lit so they know it's a house. | Counted, #twice#. I don't fret for nothing. | It is a change, fen-friend, and I don't like changes.

scene bar_the_door
when topic=home here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Dusk. I'll have #latch# on before the light goes. Always have. | I bar the door before dusk and check it after. And again before I sleep. | My chair faces the door, and the door's barred, and the lamp's lit. Then I can sit.
b : #bc_wise# | Three times? | #bc_every_night#
a : #saying#. | Three, and a prayer with the last. #oath#. | Every night of my life, fen-friend. And I'm still here.

scene dry_boards
when topic=home
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I keep #floor#, and then somebody walks the creek in on it. | A wet floor rots a house from the bottom. I've seen it, #twice#. | Twice I swept, first thing, and still a muddy print by the hearth.
b[pair.roof=yes] #household : I took my boots off. I did. | It's one print. | That one's mine, I'll own it.
b : #bc_every_time# | #bc_very_bad# | #bc_ha#
a@household : Then whose are those, #dear#? The heron's? | One print is how it starts. | Then you'll own the cloth too, and quick.
a : Boots off at the step. I've said it till I'm hoarse. | Dry boards, dry house, dry feet. That's how it goes. | I'll find whose it is. I always do.

scene gulls_screaming
when topic=animals here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #gulls.capitalize# were on the roof again at first light. Screaming like the drowned. | I can't abide a gull. Wicked eyes, and they'll have the eel off your plate. | A gull took a whole eel off the step yesterday. Off my own step, #address#.
b[job=fisher] #fisher : They follow the boats. Can't be helped. | I've lost a few to them. | Throw a stone. They learn.
b : #bc_bad_luck# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#
a@fisher : Then the boats can keep them. Not my thatch. | Thieving, like a heron at the weir. Worse. | I threw two. They laughed at me, I'd swear it.
a : I don't like a bird that laughs at you, fen-friend. | #oath#. Wicked things. | The cheek of it. My own step.

scene misty_morning
when topic=weather here.weather=fog here.time=dawn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #dawnmist.capitalize#. That's my favourite hour. The night's over and the fen's gone soft and white. | Fen-murk at dawn's a different thing from fen-murk at night, #address#. Morning murk is kindly. | I stood on the step in it with my shawl. Couldn't see the creek. Didn't need to.
b : #bc_lovely# | Is it? | #bc_ha#
a : The lights can't come in daylight. That's why I like it. | It is. Night murk hides things. Morning murk only hides the work. | #bc_lovely#. A mercy, after a long night.

scene murk_after_dark
when topic=weather here.weather=fog here.time=dusk|night
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Murk, and dark coming. I'll not go past my own step tonight. | You can't tell a lamp from #lights# in this. That's how they get you. | Somebody's out on the boards in this. I hear them. Do you hear them?
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_true# | I hear nothing.
a : Not a step, #twice#. | That's how they got my great-uncle. A lamp, he thought. | Then it's nothing. Bright One, let it be nothing.

scene riddle_lamp
when topic=pastimes
does ask.opinion / answer.detail / assess
a : Here's one for you, #address#. What's wet when it's drying? | I've one, and nobody's had it yet. What has a mouth and never eats? | Sit by #lamp# and I'll ask you one. What walks the fen and leaves no print?
b[stage=young] #pup : Ooh. A towel? | A river! | Is it a ghost?
b : I'll have to think. | #bc_who_q# | Give me a clue.
a@pup : A towel. Clever tadpole. Who taught you? | A river. Well, drown me. | It's the mist, tadpole. Not a ghost. Don't you say ghost.
a : A towel, #dear#. Think on it next time you dry your paws. | A river, #dear#. Mouth and no teeth. | The mist. Clue's in the fen-murk. Always is.

scene riddle_old
when topic=pastimes|memories self.age>=50
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : My #gran# had a riddle nobody ever answered. Took it into the fen with her. | Riddles got us through the long nights, back in my tadpole days. Riddles and the lamp. | I won a pork supper off a pedlar with a riddle once. Never told anyone the answer.
b : What was it? | #bc_lovely# | What was it?
a : I'll not say. Bad luck, a dead wolf's riddle. #oath#. | Better than fretting at the window, mind. Though I did both. | I'll not say. A riddle's only worth what nobody knows.

scene crackling
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #crackling.capitalize#. That's a feast, that is. Better than eel, and I'll say so in this house. | I had pork for the first time in a year last Restday. I nearly cried, #address#. | Get the skin dry before it goes in. That's the whole secret of crackling.
b[job=cook] #cook : Salt on the skin, too. | It's the dear meat, pork. | Dry, and a hot oven.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_good# | #bc_wise#
a@cook : Salt, aye. Fen salt. Nothing else does. | It is. Worth every copper, once in a while. | A hot oven. Not too hot. I fret about it.
a : #bc_lovely#. Don't tell them I said it about the eels. | The Bright One sends a treat now and then. | Dry. Like everything worth having in a fen.

scene lamp_prayer
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I say my prayer at the lamp every dusk. For the house, the young 'uns, and the drowned. | The Bright One has kept this house through more than I'd tell you, #address#. | I never miss Restday. Not in the wet, not with my knees. I sit by the chapel door.
b[piety=devout] #devout : The drowned too? That's kind. | And will again. | By the door? So do I.
b[piety=ordinary] #easy : That's a lot of praying. | You've been lucky. | Even with your knees?
b : #bc_bless_you# | #bc_true# | #bc_good#
a@devout : Somebody has to. They've no one else, #dear#. | #twice#, and I'll keep asking. | Back to the wall. You learn it on the fen.
a@easy : Not enough, some nights. | Lucky's not a word I use. Kept. | Especially then. Prayers on bad knees count double.
a : #saying#. | Bless you. | #blessing#.

scene child_worry
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : #self.child# was out on the water past dusk again. I sat by the lamp till I heard the boards creak. | I worry about #self.child#. I know I shouldn't. I do. | #self.child# never tells me where they're going. I find out after, and then I fret backwards.
b[stage=old] #old : They come home. They always do. | We all worry. It's the job. | Ha. Fretting backwards. I know it.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#
a@old : Till the night they don't. Bright One forgive me for saying it. | It's a job without a #wages#, that. | You'd think we'd learn, at our age.
a : Home, and dry, and the latch on. That's all I ask. | #twice#. Some nights I'm right. | Better than not fretting at all, #address#.

scene raised_three
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I raised #young#. The house still smells of eels and wet boots. | Three of them, and none of them sits with a back to the wall like I told them. | One of mine traps eels at the creek and brings them home slimy, every night. I'd not have it otherwise.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_good#
a : Every one home safe. The Bright One hears about it nightly. | Young 'uns never listen, #address#. Mine didn't. | Slimy eels on #floor#, mind. I've words about that.

scene strangers_doorway
when topic=newcomer|smalltalk
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Somebody strange out on the boards. I'll be civil from the doorway, #address#. Not past it. | A #stranger# carries things behind them. Or something follows. | Somebody I didn't know asked the way to the creek. I told them. Then I barred the door.
b : #bc_wise# | That's a bit hard. | #bc_ha#
a : Civil's free. My door isn't. | Hard, maybe. I'm still here, though. | In daylight, too. #twice#.

scene roads_never
when topic=travel
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'd not set a paw on a road these days, not for all the eel-money in the fen. | Everybody I know who went up the causeway came back different, #address#. Or didn't. | I've been #far# once, to a wedding. Bright One, never again.
b[job=carter] #road : The road's not so bad. | I've walked it a hundred times. | Most come back just fine.
b : #bc_never# | #bc_why_q# | #bc_ha#
a@road : #bandits.capitalize#, and wheel ruts, and no dyke for a mile. Not bad, you say. | And you'll walk it once too often, fen-friend. Mark me. | Fine, and full of city smoke.
a : #saying#. | They had the road in them. You could smell it. | My feet stay on the boards, thank you kindly.

scene dole_bread
when topic=times
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : To feed the #hungry# is holy work. I put a loaf by for the chapel every Restday. | Nobody on these boards should go to bed hollow while the chapel has bread, #address#. | I've been #skint#, once. I've not forgotten who fed me.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_true# | Who was it?
a : It's not much. A loaf's a loaf. | #saying#. And the fen gives back what you give. | The chapel, and the Bright One behind it. I'll not forget.

scene drink_under
when topic=smalltalk|health
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I've seen #drink# take a wolf under quicker than the fen does. I'll not have a jar in the house. | My great-uncle drank. Walked out after a light one night, soused. The fen kept him. | The taproom's a cheerful place, they tell me. So's the fen, from a distance.
b[job=innkeeper|brewer] #ale : A jar never drowned anyone who stayed indoors. | That's sad, but it's not the ale's doing. | Come and see it. It's warm.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#
a@ale : Indoors is the trick, and nobody stays there. | Ale and lights, #address#. A bad pair. | Warm's how they get you. No, thank you kindly.
a : #oath#. Not in my house. | #saying#. | Bless you, but I'll keep to my own hearth.

story the_face_in_the_light [concept=talk.lore self.age>=40 here.region=fens]
  : I was sat up one winter night, waiting on one of mine, and a light came along the dyke.
  b : One of the lights?
  : Slow, the way they come. Right up to the window, #address#. I'd not barred the door that night. The one night.
  b : #bc_and_q#
  : There was a face in it. I knew it. A wolf I grew up with, gone in the old floods.
  b : What did you do?
  : Barred the door, lit the lamp, and prayed till dawn. #oath#. I've barred it before dusk every night since.

story the_flood_child [concept=talk.memories self.age>=50 here.region=fens]
  : I was a tadpole when the fen rose over the low boards in one night. #olddays.capitalize#, we call it now.
  b : Were you frightened?
  : I sat on the roof with my #mum# and watched the fen come into the house. Wet floors. I've hated them since.
  b : #bc_poor_soul#
  : In the morning there were new lights on the fen. More than before. Nobody would say why.
  b : Oh.
  : #saying#. I knew why. I was a tadpole, but I knew.

story the_pedlar_riddle [concept=talk.pastimes]
  : A pedlar came up the boards once and bet me a pork supper I couldn't stump him.
  b : Did you?
  : I asked him what walks the fen and leaves no print. He thought a whole hour, #address#.
  b : #bc_and_q#
  : He paid up. Best #crackling# I ever ate.
  b : What's the answer?
  : I'll not tell you either. You can bet me a supper. #bc_ha#

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Stay on the boards, please, and say what you want. | #greet#. #talk_open# I'm listening, but I'm watching the light.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Come in, quick, and I'll bar the door. | #topic.player#. You're a welcome face. #talk_open#
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=dusk|night] : It's getting dark, #address#. Say it quick, I'm barring up. | Not now, not after dusk. Well. Quickly, then.
dlg @1 resident.job : I keep the house. Floors, food, #latch# and lamp. That's work enough at my age. | I keep the house for #young#. #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.news : #news_none# I don't go far enough to hear any. | Nothing I'd want to repeat, #address#. The Bright One keep us.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Straight home, and don't follow any lights. | #blessing#. Mind the boards.
graft resident.hub
choice Are the lights on the fen really the drowned? [here.region=fens] -> lights
node lights
say They are. I've seen faces in them. Folk say marsh gas. Folk haven't sat by the window all night with the latch off.
mood worried
free
choice Whose faces? -> lights_who
choice I'll keep away from them. -> hub
node lights_who
say Some I knew. Some from before my time. I'll not say names. Bar your door before dusk, and keep a lamp lit. That's all I'll say.
choice I will. Thank you. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


old
line @1 tell.self : At my age the knees decide where I go. Mostly they say the fire. | Seventy winters, #address#, and still I check the latch twice.
line @1 give.advice : Bar the door before you need to, #dear#. I'll not be here forever to tell you. | Never follow a light. Never. That's an old wolf's whole wisdom.
scene old_knees
when topic=health self.stage=old
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My knees are #hurt# in the damp, and it's always damp. | I had the fen-ague all last month. I lit the lamp every night in case it was the end. | I sleep sitting up now, facing the door. The young 'uns laugh. Let them.
b[job=healer] #healer : Willow bark for the knees. | You're stronger than you think. | Lie down, or your back will go too.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_ha#
a@healer : #remedy.capitalize#. I've drunk enough to grow a tree. | Strong as a reed in a blow, #address#. Bends, doesn't break. | Lie down with my back to the door? Never.
a : Seventy winters. They've earned their aching. | It wasn't the end. The Bright One wasn't ready for me. | They'll do the same at my age. Mark me.

scene old_floods_remembered
when topic=memories self.stage=old here.region=fens
does tell.memory / react.story / assess
a : I remember the old boards, before they raised them. Water on the floor every spring. | When I was young, the drowned bell still rang some nights. You don't hear it now. Or I don't. | My #mum# barred the door before dusk, and her #mum# before her. I learned it at the latch.
b[stage=old] #old : I remember those boards. Cold feet all spring. | I heard it once. Never forgot it. | Mine did the same.
b : Wet floors every spring? | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_wise#
a@old : Cold feet, wet floors, and nobody complained. We'd no breath for it. | Nor me, fen-friend. Nor me. | Then you'll know. Some things you keep.
a : Every spring. That's why I can't abide them now. | Maybe I've gone deaf. Maybe they've stopped. I don't know which I'd rather. | #saying#. My young 'uns will learn it yet.
